 "about": "A realm's edits (edits.proto, GitHub #13250): the bodies that change a realm through coax/web/api/realms.c, as the realm edit layer and My Realm send them (no revision) and as the CLI sends them under .../edit-v1/ (the revision first), with the status and body the server answers today. \"rev\" names the realm whose revision the body's \"rev\":41 stands for: the check reads it from the realm's spec, and the revision in the answer is the run's (\"vary\"). \"bodies\" are requests the planner's model answers (an ask, a revision, an ask marked done): only their bodies are held here. aethyr/forge/change.coax writes every body; aethyr/forge/change-goldens.coax holds them and the answers' keys; coax/web/api/tests/realm_record_checks.coax makes the calls.",
